  "details": "Proposal:\n\nCurrently, when a VRChat+ subscription expires, the badge disappears completely. This means that past supporters lose any visible recognition of their contribution, which may reduce their motivation to renew their subscription.\n\n Suggested Changes:\n\n1. Instead of completely removing the badge, replace it with a \"former supporter\" version (e.g., a gray star or another visual indicator).\n\n2. Make the badge dynamic based on subscription status:\n\n  -Active subscriber → Gold badge (current system).\n\n  -Former subscriber → Gray badge (or another visual variation).\n\n  -Never subscribed → No badge (same as now).\n\n3. Benefits of this approach:\n\n  -Encourages past subscribers to return since they still feel connected to VRChat+.\n\n  -Attracts new subscribers by making the badge more visible in the community, leading \n\nto increased interest in VRChat+.\n\n  -Strengthens community loyalty, as users who supported VRChat financially receive long-term recognition.\n\nThis change would improve user engagement, increase subscriptions, and enhance the perceived value of VRChat+.",
